<title>INDIA: India Sterlite 95/96 net 1.4 bln rupees.</title>
<headline>India Sterlite 95/96 net 1.4 bln rupees.</headline>
<dateline>BOMBAY 1996-09-30</dateline>
<text>
<p>Year to June 30, 1996</p>
<p>	     (in million rupees unless stated)</p>
<p>			  Premerger     Postmerger</p>
<p>   Net profit	  1,316.0	 1,401.6    vs   1,148.7</p>
<p>   Net sales	   8,071.5	10,066.7    vs   7,208.9</p>
<p>			  Premerger     Postmerger</p>
<p>   Other income	  276.8	    288.2   vs	347.5</p>
<p>   Expenditure	 6,765.1	  8,663.9   vs    6.067.2</p>
<p>   Interest		 79.5	     92.2   vs	129.7</p>
<p>   Gross profit	1,503.7	  1,598.8   vs    1,359.5</p>
<p>   Depreciation	  166.6	    176.1   vs	150.8</p>
<p>   Tax			21.1	     21.1   vs	 60.0</p>
<p>   Share (in rupees)    31.6	     31.6   vs	 28.5</p>
<p>Note: Sterlite Industries said in a note the scheme of merger of Sterlite Communications with the company which had been approved by shareholders of both the companies will be effective from April 1, 1996. Thus, the post-merger figures include operations of Sterlite Communications. The merger is pending before the High Court for its sanction, it said</p>
<p>-- Bombay newsroom 91-22-265 9000</p>
</text>
